.TH QFW-SINFO 1 "September 2026" "qfw-slurm 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-sinfo \- show Slurm service hosts and QPM state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-sinfo
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ node ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-sinfo
connects to the QFw site directory as a DEFw client, reads the sanitized QPM
service summary, and combines it with
.BR sinfo (1)
JSON output.
The Slurm host state and logical QPM state are reported separately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write a versioned JSON object instead of the terminal table.
.TP
.BI \-\-site-config " path"
Use the named QFw site configuration.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " seconds"
Bound each required data-source operation.  The default is 10 seconds.
.TP
.I node
Show detailed state for one QPM or DVM service node.
.SH STATES
IDLE identifies a ready QPM without active reservations.  BUSY identifies a
ready QPM with active reservations and does not imply that admission is
closed.  DOWN identifies an absent, unreachable, or unready QPM.  MAINT
identifies administrative maintenance state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QFW_SITE_CONFIG
Default QFw site configuration.
.TP
.B DEFW_PREFIX
Activated DEFw installation containing
.BR defwp (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates complete output.  One indicates partial output caused by a
failed required data source.  Two indicates invalid command syntax.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
source /opt/openqse/qfw/bin/qfw-activate \
    --venv /opt/openqse/qfw-venv
qfw-sinfo
qfw-sinfo nwqsim-head
qfw-sinfo --json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sinfo (1),
.BR qfw-squeue (1),
.BR qfw-slurm (7)
